{"purpose":"Define the development workflow rules for the eka project: branch strategy, worktree isolation, merge policy, and owner privileges.","content":"1. All implementation MUST be done on a new branch created from the develop branch (feature/*, fix/*, refactor/*, docs/*, chore/*) — never directly on main. 2. Heavy work MAY be done in a separate git worktree, so the primary worktree stays isolated from un-fixed changes. 3. Merging to main MUST come from the develop branch through a GitHub pull request. 4. Exception (owner only): the project owner — name 'Marij Mokoginta' (git config user.name) or email 'marijmokoginta04@gmail.com' — MAY push directly to main or open a pull request from a branch other than develop. Everyone else is strictly forbidden from direct pushes to main and from non-develop pull requests."}